spec: specs/persist.md, the last open Behavior box

why: the box names an INDEX the file engine never had (segments carry
  their base offset in the header; reads scan within a segment). What
  the engine does have is a derived in-memory segment list refreshed
  from the directory — that is the invariant worth proving.

what: read Segments/FileStore for what refresh actually guarantees;
  a test on the real invariant (the directory decides: a segment
  appearing or vanishing behind an open store is seen by reads); the
  box rewritten to what is built, with the no-index decision recorded.

next: worktree, read refresh, write the test
